lines += ['', 'For the current data, the positive KOSPI Transformer exception must remain visible; it is not LNN evidence. The LNN-wide superiority/conditional-generalization claim is not strengthened. The evaluation-design and benchmark/negative-results framing remains appropriate, with a clearly qualified isolated positive exception. Nikkei High has weak two-sided PT and inferior hit rate to Always-Up, consistent with retaining it as descriptive and statistically fragile rather than established generalization. This conclusion does not show equivalence/no signal, and negative relationships must not be inverted without a new prespecified evaluation.', '', 'All source artifacts and selections remain unchanged. Conventional PT, block-bootstrap sensitivity, episode-aware permutation and reduced-overlap results have distinct assumptions; no one favorable test is used to override the rest.']
